# Fake News Detection — Full Stack ML Web App

## Goal
Build a complete production-quality Fake News Detection web application using Flask + Scikit-learn + Vanilla JS.

## Proposed Changes

### Root Files
#### [NEW] app.py — Flask backend with REST API
#### [NEW] train_model.py — ML training pipeline
#### [NEW] requirements.txt
#### [NEW] README.md

### ML Pipeline
- Load Fake.csv + True.csv from dataset/
- Clean and preprocess text (lowercase, strip HTML, punctuation removal, stopwords)
- TF-IDF Vectorization (max 50k features)
- Logistic Regression classifier
- Save model + vectorizer to model/ via Joblib

### Templates (Jinja2)
- index.html — Landing page with hero, features, about, contact
- dashboard.html — Charts (Chart.js), stats cards
- history.html — Prediction history with search/delete
- about.html — Team + tech info
- contact.html — Contact form

### Static Assets
- static/css/style.css — Global design system (dark/light mode, glassmorphism)
- static/js/main.js — Shared utilities (dark mode, animations)
- static/js/detector.js — News detection logic
- static/js/dashboard.js — Chart.js dashboard
- static/js/history.js — History management

### Backend API Routes
- POST /api/predict — Run prediction
- GET /api/history — Fetch all predictions
- DELETE /api/history/<id> — Delete entry
- GET /api/stats — Dashboard statistics

